WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.420
How does a protein turn force into ionic current?

2
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.760
One leading model, still debated, says the answer is a shape.

3
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:19.740
In purified mouse PIEZO2, curved blades bow the membrane into a dome.

4
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.620
The dome is about 28 nanometres across.

5
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.300
Flatten it, and a pore in its centre opens.

6
00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:29.913
Here is the geometry.

7
00:00:30.793 --> 00:00:35.973
A curved cap of fixed surface area projects less area onto the plane of the

8
00:00:35.973 --> 00:00:39.753
membrane. The same cap, flattened, projects more.

9
00:00:40.553 --> 00:00:43.373
So flattening increases projected area.

10
00:00:44.253 --> 00:00:48.453
Anything that favours more projected area favours the flat state.

11
00:00:49.317 --> 00:00:51.477
Now add tension in the membrane.

12
00:00:52.477 --> 00:00:57.277
Tension lowers the energy of a state in proportion to its larger projected area.

13
00:00:57.937 --> 00:01:02.297
So as tension rises, the larger-area, flat state is favoured.

14
00:01:03.177 --> 00:01:07.477
The energy change is minus tension times the change in projected area.

15
00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.627
What is the evidence?

16
00:01:10.547 --> 00:01:16.287
Purified mouse PIEZO1 in artificial droplet bilayers with no other cellular

17
00:01:16.287 --> 00:01:19.187
components, was still activated by force.

18
00:01:19.547 --> 00:01:23.167
So protein plus lipid is sufficient in that preparation.

19
00:01:24.187 --> 00:01:30.627
In liposome vesicles, cryo-EM sorted purified mouse PIEZO1 into curved and

20
00:01:30.627 --> 00:01:31.627
flattened classes.

21
00:01:32.287 --> 00:01:36.687
They differ by roughly 300 square nanometres of in-plane expansion.

22
00:01:36.687 --> 00:01:40.607
The authors hedge whether that is the gating transition itself.

23
00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:43.110
Now the arithmetic.

24
00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:50.390
Lewis and Grandl pressurised patches of mouse PIEZO1 in a human cell line, and

25
00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:51.750
measured the patch radius.

26
00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:58.050
Take an illustrative patch, 2 micrometres in radius, under 2000 pascals.

27
00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:02.430
Tension is radius times pressure, divided by 2.

28
00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:05.810
That gives 2 millinewtons per metre.

29
00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:12.650
Their fit has a half activation tension of 2.7 and a slope of 0.8.

30
00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:18.190
At 2.0, the fit predicts about 29 percent of the plateau current.

31
00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:21.763
Force could also arrive through protein.

32
00:02:22.543 --> 00:02:26.943
A tether of cadherin and actin has been proposed, from cultured cells.

33
00:02:27.663 --> 00:02:29.563
These two accounts are not rivals.

34
00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:35.263
Sufficiency in a bilayer cannot exclude a coupling route in an intact cell.

35
00:02:36.043 --> 00:02:40.123
A tether in cultured cells cannot abolish the lipid energetics.

36
00:02:40.923 --> 00:02:46.703
Keep this rule: sufficient in one preparation does not mean exclusive in another.
